{"diagnosis": "Loopback divider 64 send 0xa5 traps with `TRAP: uart timeout, no byte received` and tohost FAIL 0xdead, meaning recv_buf_valid never asserted vs expected 0xa5 received. Excerpt shows duplicate `1:` labels at lines 78 and 83 with no `0:` idle case, so reset state 0 falls to default and the `if (!ser_rx)` start-bit detector is unreachable. CONE_SLICE offers no simpleuart provenance, so trace wins.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -77,7 +77,7 @@
 			case (recv_state)
-				1: begin
+				0: begin
 					if (!ser_rx)
 						recv_state <= 1;
 					recv_divcnt <= 0;
 				end
 				1: begin", "expected": "tohost PASS with byte 0xa5 received, no TRAP timeout — re-sim must not show FAIL 0xdead"}

